      "type": "/type/text",
      "value": "1.1 IN A RAILROAD CAR AT NIGHTFALL, WHEN the natural light outside has diminished until it is even with the artificial light inside, the passenger facing forward sees in his window two images at once: the dim landscape rushing toward him out of a pit of darkness, and the interior of the car, reflected with its more or less motionless occupants."
